@@ -153,6 +153,32 @@ The following directives are provided for module and class contents:
       Describe the location where the object is defined.  The default value is
       the module specified by :rst:dir:`py:currentmodule`.
 
+.. rst:directive:: .. py:type:: name
+
+   Describes a type alias.  The optional ``canonical`` option gives the type
+   represented by the alias; it appears after the alias name in the signature
+   and is parsed as a Python annotation.  A description body is supported.
+
+   .. code-block:: rst
+
+      .. py:type:: UserId
+         :canonical: int
+
+         Identifier assigned to a user.
+
+   .. rubric:: options
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: canonical
+      :type: type expression
+
+      Describe the type represented by the alias.  The expression is optional
+      and may contain references to other Python types.
+
+.. rst:role:: py:type
+
+   Reference a type alias declared with :rst:dir:`py:type`.  Dotted names may
+   be used, and references resolve using the normal Python-domain lookup rules.
+
 .. rst:directive:: .. py:exception:: name
                    .. py:exception:: name(parameters)
                    .. py:exception:: name[type parameters](parameters)
